   "text": "The observed pattern is matched by the quadruple perovskite CaFe4(CuO4)3 (mp-1640048) alone.\n\n1. **Observed peaks.** Above the noise there are four clear reflections:\n\n   | 2\u03b8 (\u00b0) | d-spacing (\u00c5) | Intensity |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | \u224833.95 | 2.638 | 100 |\n   | \u224848.8 | 1.865 | 19 |\n   | \u224860.8 | \u2014 | 33 |\n   | \u224871.5 | \u2014 | 11 |\n\n   The positions of the 60.8\u00b0 and 71.5\u00b0 peaks were estimated, not read point by point.\n\n2. **Lattice.** The ratio of the first two d-spacings is \u221a2. Together with the other two positions, this fits a perovskite-type cubic sub-cell with pseudo-cubic a \u2248 3.73 \u00c5. The four peaks index as (110), (200), (211) and (220) of that sub-cell.\n\n3. **Matching candidate.** The CaFe4(CuO4)3 cell is body-centred with primitive edge 6.44 \u00c5. That gives a conventional cell of a \u2248 6.44 \u00d7 2/\u221a3 \u2248 7.44 \u00c5, which is twice 3.72 \u00c5.\n   - Its (220), (400), (422) and (440) reflections fall at about 34.0\u00b0, 48.9\u00b0, 60.9\u00b0 and 71.7\u00b0.\n   - These match the four observed peaks.\n   - Its superstructure reflections, such as (211) near 29\u00b0 and (222) near 42\u00b0, are expected to be weak. They would sit within the noise floor, consistent with their absence.\n\n4. **Rejected candidates.** The other cells checked give peaks in the wrong places.\n   - Ba2PrNbO6 has pseudo-cubic a \u2248 4.38 \u00c5, putting peaks near 28.8\u00b0 and 41.2\u00b0.\n   - CsLaNb2O7 has a \u2248 3.95 \u00c5, putting peaks near 32.0\u00b0 and 45.9\u00b0.\n   - Nd2BiO2 converts to a tetragonal cell of a \u2248 4.02, c \u2248 14.07 \u00c5, giving peaks near 31.4\u00b0 and 36.9\u00b0.\n\n   The remaining candidates were not checked peak by peak.\n\n5. **Second phase.** No unexplained peaks remain, so I see no evidence of a second phase.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-1640048\"], \"confidence\": 0.8, \"note\": \"The four observed peaks (\u224833.95, 48.8, 60.8, 71.5\u0